From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: keep the accounting session and EAPOL state of a
 moved association

Depends on 836-AP-MLD-keep-the-association-of-a-non-AP-MLD-at-a-lin.patch
and 868-AP-MLD-keep-the-session-timers-of-a-moved-associatio.patch.

Each affiliated STA of a non-AP MLD runs an accounting session of its
own: ieee802_1x_ml_set_sta_authorized() authorizes the link STAs, and
each starts a session with its own Acct-Session-Id. Only the
association STA has an EAPOL state machine, so only its session carries
the User-Name, Class and Chargeable-User-Identity of the EAP
authentication; the sessions of the link STAs name the MAC address.

When the association moves to another link, at an AP removal of the
association link or at a Link Reconfiguration that deletes it, the
caller frees the old association STA. ap_free_sta() sends an
Accounting-Stop for the session with the EAP identity, and
ieee802_1x_free_station() frees the EAPOL state machine. The non-AP MLD
stays associated, but the RADIUS server sees the session of its user
end, and the AP no longer reauthenticates it at eap_reauth_period.

Move both to the new association STA in hostapd_ml_move_assoc_sta():
- accounting_sta_move() ends the session that the new association STA
  started for its own link, and gives that STA the session of the old
  one: Acct-Session-Id, start time, counters and interim settings. The
  interim update timer keeps its remaining time.
- ieee802_1x_move_station() gives the new STA the EAPOL state machine.
  The links share the authenticator, so only the STA of the state
  machine changes. The RADIUS User-Name and CUI of the STA move with it.

ap_free_sta() of the old STA then has no session to stop and no state
machine to free.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/accounting.c
+++ b/src/ap/accounting.c
@@ -572,6 +572,38 @@ void accounting_mld_first_bss_moved(stru
 						   accounting_interim_error_cb,
 						   first);
 }
+
+
+/* The session that the association STA of a non-AP MLD started goes on in
+ * the STA that becomes its association STA. That STA started a session for
+ * its own link, which ends. */
+void accounting_sta_move(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
+			 struct hostapd_data *new_hapd,
+			 struct sta_info *new_sta)
+{
+	if (!sta->acct_session_started)
+		return;
+
+	accounting_sta_stop(new_hapd, new_sta);
+	ap_sta_move_timeout(accounting_interim_update, hapd, sta, new_hapd,
+			    new_sta);
+	new_sta->acct_session_id = sta->acct_session_id;
+	new_sta->acct_session_start = sta->acct_session_start;
+	new_sta->acct_terminate_cause = sta->acct_terminate_cause;
+	new_sta->acct_interim_interval = sta->acct_interim_interval;
+	new_sta->acct_interim_errors = sta->acct_interim_errors;
+	new_sta->last_rx_bytes_hi = sta->last_rx_bytes_hi;
+	new_sta->last_rx_bytes_lo = sta->last_rx_bytes_lo;
+	new_sta->last_tx_bytes_hi = sta->last_tx_bytes_hi;
+	new_sta->last_tx_bytes_lo = sta->last_tx_bytes_lo;
+	new_sta->acct_session_started = 1;
+	sta->acct_session_started = 0;
+	hostapd_logger(new_hapd, new_sta->addr, HOSTAPD_MODULE_RADIUS,
+		       HOSTAPD_LEVEL_INFO,
+		       "moved accounting session %016llX from link %u",
+		       (unsigned long long) new_sta->acct_session_id,
+		       hapd->mld_link_id);
+}
